@bank all
// Head writer 4, for the career system (design-doc "Leave, missed shifts and being let go", 2026-10-17), on the
// Career engineer's keys (claude/leave, 0.61.x). Friends' lines: worried.chief (after Calder's talk),
// worried.captain (after the Captain's reprimand), worried.last (at the very bottom), farewell.eve (the day before
// you leave), farewell.day (your last day and the shuttle-bay send-off). Extras the engine may use later:
// career.missed, career.up, career.leave.booked, career.onleave, career.back.
// TEXTS are shown by the game, said by nobody: no tokens but {me}. Mails and the card are "subject | body".
// Keep them free of exact counts (the lead's defaults may change): "a few", "every few weeks".

== career.tip.leave
- Need a day? Book leave in Schedule on your device, by 07:30 that day at the latest.
- You get a few leave days, and one more every few weeks. Cancel a booking to get it back.
- Time in the infirmary when you're ill never uses up leave or counts as missed.

== career.tip.late
- Late for your shift. A little late is only a small dip. Be in the Works bay by 09:00.

== career.tip.missed
- You missed a shift without leave: a big hit to your work standing. Book leave instead.

== career.tip.chief
- Chief Calder has sent for you. To climb back: be on shift by 09:00 and turn in jobs.

== career.tip.captain
- The Captain has sent for you. One more step down and you're sent home. It's not too late.

== career.tip.bottom
- At the very bottom. A few days like this and you're let go. One good shift turns it round.

== career.tip.notice
- You've been let go. Tomorrow is your last day aboard. Friends will want to say goodbye.

== career.tip.up
- Your work standing is climbing. Keep turning up. People have noticed.

== career.tip.clock
- Clock in by the tea corner at shift start, out at the end. Leave and sick days need none.

== clock.auto
- The clock signed you out at 17:00. It does that.
- 17:00. The clock signed you out for you. Go and eat.
- Shift over: the clock signed you out at 17:00.

== career.mail.chief
- My office | Come to my office, Deck 5, today. Missed shifts. We'll talk it through.

== career.mail.captain
- Ready room | The Captain will see you in her ready room, Deck 1. Please be prompt.

== career.mail.notice
- Your last day | The Wren is letting you go. The Tern leaves tomorrow. I'm sorry.

== career.card
- The Wren sails on | Your time on the Wren is over, {me}. Thank you for it.
- The Wren sails on | A scrubber hums. Nobody thanks the air. Thank you, {me}.

// Crew who know you a little: the everyday lines. Friends (the ten voices) and the story crew have their own.
== worried.chief
? tier>=colleague
- Heard the Chief had a word. She's fair. Do what she said and it's done.
- Calder only says it once, plainly. That's a kindness, believe it or not.

== worried.captain
? tier>=colleague
- Up to the ready room? {sigh}. The Captain's kind. Still, go to your shift.   #warm

== worried.last
? tier>=colleague
- People are saying they'll send you home if this goes on. Please don't let them.   #warm

== farewell.eve
? tier>=acquaintance
- I heard you're leaving tomorrow. I'm sorry. Look after yourself.
- Tomorrow, is it? The Wren won't be the same. Safe trip.
? tier>=colleague
- Leaving tomorrow. I'm sorry it went this way. You were good company.   #warm

== farewell.day
? tier>=acquaintance
- {bye}, {nick}. Safe trip on the Tern.
- Off today, then. Good luck out there. I mean it.
? tier>=colleague
- Go well. Turn up wherever you land. The rest comes.   #warm
? tier>=friend
- Came to find you. Couldn't let today go without it.   #warm
- Window seat. Promise me.   #warm
- Write when you land. Proper Mail.   #warm

== career.missed
? tier>=acquaintance
- {hi}. Didn't see you on shift today. All right?
- Missed shift, I heard. Happens once. Just don't make it a habit.
? tier>=colleague
- If something's keeping you from shift, say. Someone here can help.   #warm

== career.up
? tier>=colleague
- Saw you on shift this morning. Good. Keep that up.
- Things looking up? You look more like yourself.

== career.leave.booked
? tier>=acquaintance
- Day off tomorrow? Good for you. Sleep in.
- Leave tomorrow! Anything planned, or just nothing at all?

== career.onleave
? tier>=acquaintance
- Aren't you on leave? Go and do something nice.
- On leave and you're still here? Fair. Where else would you go?   #funny

== career.back
? tier>=acquaintance
- {hi}. Back from leave? You look rested.
- Welcome back. The board missed you. Well, someone had to say it.   #funny
